petrus-simulation
Copyright 2026 Seasoned

This package is a Haskell port of the bounded simulation runner and the
simulation HTTP service of Petrus (petrus.simulation and
petrus.simulation_http, by Henrique Bastos), pinned under upstream/petrus and
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. It follows the runner's
implementation-free-v1 profile and spec/simulation-http-v1.md, and its test
suite ports the upstream tests in tests/petrus/engine/test_simulation.py and
tests/petrus/engine/test_simulation_http.py together with the fixture
scenario of tests/simulation_support.py. The package itself is licensed under
the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).

The test and benchmark scripts in test/ and bench/ run the upstream Petrus
code from its pinned virtual environment to record the reference behavior;
no upstream source is included in the library.

Through petrus-http-core, the service reproduces the observable behavior of
CPython's http.server, urllib.parse and ipaddress (the Python Software
Foundation License); no CPython source code is included.
